@startuml
title Student authentication - HTTP, Provider and Session composition (design only)
actor Student
participant "Auth UI" as UI
participant "Auth HTTP Adapter" as HTTP
participant "Auth Application" as App
participant "Google OIDC Adapter" as OIDC
participant "Google OIDC Provider" as Google
participant "Turnstile Adapter" as Bot
participant "Magic Mail Adapter" as Mail
database "Main D1 / Auth Transaction Port" as D1

UI -> HTTP: GET /api/auth/student/csrf (same-origin)
HTTP -> D1: Read/create fixed-expiry pre-auth
HTTP --> UI: 200 CSRF token + Host pre-auth Cookie
alt Google
  UI -> HTTP: POST google/start + Origin / pre-auth CSRF
  HTTP -> App: Validated start
  App -> D1: Rate check; supersede old flow/proof; store state / nonce / verifier
  App --> UI: 200 authorizationUrl with S256 PKCE
  UI -> Google: Top-level authorization navigation
  Google -> HTTP: GET callback code + state
  HTTP -> App: Validate wire and Browser Cookie
  App -> D1: Assert state / pre-auth / purpose / expiry; claim once
  D1 --> App: Claim committed (never restored)
  App -> OIDC: Claimed flow / code / saved verifier
  OIDC -> Google: HTTPS code exchange; trusted signing keys
  Google --> OIDC: Provider response
  OIDC -> OIDC: Verify signature / claims / nonce; discard raw tokens
  OIDC --> App: Verified issuer / subject / email OR abstract failure
  note over App, OIDC
    No external call inside D1 batch.
    No automatic Google Login retry.
    Wrong state/browser does not terminate another valid flow.
  end note
else Magic Link
  UI -> HTTP: POST magic/request {email, turnstileToken, invitationToken?}
  HTTP -> App: Validated Origin / pre-auth CSRF
  App -> D1: Reserve source rate budget
  App -> Bot: Server token / hostname / action verification
  Bot --> App: verified / rejected / unavailable
  App -> D1: Reserve destination budget; decide purpose; supersede and store hash
  D1 --> App: Committed OR no-send with same accepted outcome
  HTTP --> UI: 202 accepted (no enumeration or delivery result)
  opt Committed sendable Challenge
    App -> Mail: Post-response best-effort send; memory-only token
    Mail --> Student: /student/login/magic#token=...
  end
  Student -> UI: Open link; remove fragment; preview and explicitly confirm
  UI -> HTTP: POST magic/consume {token} + current Browser pre-auth CSRF
  HTTP -> App: Validate current Browser, token format and purpose
end

alt Provider / Challenge valid; existing binding or verified contact match
  App -> D1: One batch: assert flow / binding / latest access; consume; issue NEW Session
  D1 -> D1: Initial + final section 8.4 issuance predicate; full rollback on failure
  D1 --> App: Commit
  App --> HTTP: Authenticated result (no Account ID or provider token)
  HTTP --> UI: Session Cookie; Google 303 /student or Magic 200 next=student
else Valid new identity
  App -> D1: Consume flow + save Browser-bound proof with original expiry
  HTTP --> UI: Google 303 /student/register or Magic 200 next=registration
  UI -> HTTP: GET registration (same-origin pre-auth)
  HTTP --> UI: 200 Server-verified email
  Student -> UI: Enter name and confirm
  UI -> HTTP: POST registration {name} + Origin / pre-auth CSRF
  HTTP -> App: Server proof only; no client identity / role
  App -> D1: Recheck binding; for NEW Student recheck current mode and Invitation
  D1 -> D1: One batch: proof / Invitation consume, Student / Account / binding, Session guards
  D1 --> App: Commit OR all-or-nothing rollback
  HTTP --> UI: 201 + NEW Session Cookie OR safe error
else Invalid / unavailable
  App --> HTTP: Stable safe Application Error
  HTTP --> UI: Safe JSON or fixed Google failure redirect; no raw error / token
end

UI -> HTTP: Business request with Session Cookie; unsafe also Origin / Session CSRF
HTTP -> D1: section 8.3 latest Session / role / lifecycle / access
HTTP --> UI: Authorized result OR 401 / 403 / 503
UI -> HTTP: POST logout {} + Origin / Session CSRF
HTTP -> D1: Revoke only this Session; assert final revocation
D1 --> HTTP: Confirmed server revocation OR unavailable
HTTP --> UI: 204 + Cookie removal OR 503 (no success assumption)
@enduml
